body:
OpenVINO Version 2023.0-2023.3 Operating System Ubuntu 22.04 (LTS) Device used for inference GPU Framework None Model used None Issue description We encountered an output problem with one of our models. After isolating the problem, we found that if the input is greater than 2048, the matmul operation returns incorrect output. Also, this problem did not occur prior to 2023.0. Step-by-step reproduction Execute the following code. import openvino.runtime as ov import numpy as np  def create_matmul_model(size):     input_data1 = ov.opset10.parameter([1, 1, size], ov.Type.f32)     input_data2 = ov.opset10.parameter([1, size, 1], ov.Type.f32)     output = ov.opset10.matmul(data_a=input_data1,                                 data_b=input_data2,                                 transpose_a=False,                                 transpose_b=False)     model = ov.Model([output], [input_data1, input_data2], "model")     return model  core = ov.Core()  input_size = (2048, 2049)  for size in input_size:     model = create_matmul_model(size)     compiled_cpu_model = core.compile_model(model, "CPU")     compiled_gpu_model = core.compile_model(model, "GPU")     cpu_infer_request = compiled_cpu_model.create_infer_request()     gpu_infer_request = compiled_gpu_model.create_infer_request()      input_1_name = model.inputs[0].any_name     input_2_name = model.inputs[1].any_name     input_1 = np.ones((1, 1, size), np.float32)     input_2 = np.ones((1, size, 1), np.float32)     input_ = {input_1_name: input_1,               input_2_name: input_2}      cpu_pred = cpu_infer_request.infer(input_)     gpu_pred = gpu_infer_request.infer(input_)     cpu_result = list(cpu_pred.values())[0]     gpu_result = list(gpu_pred.values())[0]     eq = np.all(cpu_result == gpu_result)     print(f"input size: {size}
"           f"output is {'same' if eq else 'different'}
"           f"cpu_result_max_value: {cpu_result.max()}
"           f"gpu_result_max_value: {gpu_result.max()}
") Relevant log output on 2023.3 input size: 2048 output is same cpu_result_max_value: 2048.0 gpu_result_max_value: 2048.0  input size: 2049 output is different cpu_result_max_value: 2049.0 gpu_result_max_value: 2048.0  on 2022.3.1 input size: 2048 output is same cpu_result_max_value: 2048.0 gpu_result_max_value: 2048.0  input size: 2049 output is same cpu_result_max_value: 2049.0 gpu_result_max_value: 2049.0  Issue submission checklist   I'm reporting an issue. It's not a question.  I checked the problem with the documentation, FAQ, open issues, Stack Overflow, etc., and have not found a solution.  There is reproducer code and related data files such as images, videos, models, etc.

OpenVINO Version 2024.1.0 Operating System Ubuntu 20.04 (LTS) Device used for inference CPU Framework ONNX Model used custom model Issue description I want to slice a vector inside a model on a dynamic dimension using openvino 2024.1.0. I don't see any problem for this in the doc regarding the cpu plugin, as it happened in 2023 version (see this). But I get this error: "Exception from src/plugins/intel_cpu/src/node.cpp:87: Unexpected: CPU plug-in doesn't support If operation with dynamic rank. Operation name: /If" The node.cpp file  at these lines checks if the output shape rank is dynamic and in that case throws the exception:     if (typeStr != "Result" && typeStr != "Assign") {         if (op->get_output_size() == 0) {             OPENVINO_THROW("Node with type '", typeStr, "' and name '", name, "' does not have any outputs.");         }         for (size_t i = 0; i < op->get_output_size(); i++) {             const auto &shape = op->get_output_partial_shape(i);             if (shape.rank().is_dynamic()) {                 OPENVINO_THROW("Unexpected: CPU plug-in doesn't support ",                                getTypeStr(),                                " operation with dynamic rank. Operation name: ",                                getName());             }              bool isScalar = shape.rank().get_length() == 0;             outputShapes.emplace_back(isScalar ? ov::PartialShape{1} : shape);             originalOutputPrecisions.emplace_back(op->get_output_element_type(i));         }          childEdges.reserve(outputShapes.size());     }  Thanks! Step-by-step reproduction Model Definition import torch.nn as nn import torch   class Model(nn.Module):     def __init__(self,a):         super().__init__()         self.scale=a       def forward(self,x,first_index,last_index):              first_index=first_index.squeeze(0)         last_index=last_index.squeeze(0)           x=x*self.scale          y=x[:,first_index:last_index,:]         s=y.sum()          return s  Notebook import torch from model_simple import Model import openvino as ov import numpy as np import onnxruntime as ort  a=3 x=torch.randn([1,10,3], dtype=torch.float32)  ini=torch.tensor(2).unsqueeze(0) end=torch.tensor(10).unsqueeze(0)  model = Model(a) model.eval()  y1=model(x,ini,end) print(f"Python: {y1}
")   print("Compiling onnx")  torch.onnx.export(model,               # model being run                     (x,ini,end),                         # model input (or a tuple for multiple inputs)                     "model_simple.onnx",            # where to save the model (can be a file or file-like object)                     verbose=False,                     export_params=True,        # store the trained parameter weights inside the model file                     #   opset_version=20,          # the ONNX version to export the model to                     do_constant_folding=True,  # whether to execute constant folding for optimization                     input_names = ['input1','input2','input3'],   # the model's input names                     output_names = ['output1'], # the model's output names                     dynamic_axes={                         'input1' : {0 : 'batch_size', 1: 'chunk_length'},    # variable length axes                         'input2' : {0 : 'batch_size'},                         'input3' : {0 : 'batch_size'},                         }                     ) # Inference session session = ort.InferenceSession("model_simple.onnx")  # Info input_name1 = session.get_inputs()[0].name input_name2 = session.get_inputs()[1].name input_name3 = session.get_inputs()[2].name output_names = session.get_outputs()[0].name print(input_name1,input_name2, input_name3, output_names)    # Run output = session.run(None, {'input1': x.numpy(), 'input2': ini.numpy(), 'input3': end.numpy()})  print(f"ONNX: {output}
")  ov_model = ov.convert_model("model_simple.onnx",                             verbose=False,                             share_weights=False,                             input=([("input1", [-1, -1, 3]),("input2", [-1,1]),("input3", [-1,1])]),                             output=["output1"]                             )  ov.save_model(ov_model, 'model_simple.xml', compress_to_fp16=True) del ov_model  config = {"INFERENCE_PRECISION_HINT": 'f32'} ov_compiled_model = ov.compile_model('model_simple.xml', "CPU", config=config)  x2=np.random.randn(1,10,3).astype(np.float32) ini2=np.array([[2]]) end2=np.array([[10]]) y2=ov_compiled_model(x2,ini2,end2) print(f"Openvino: {y2}
")    x3=np.random.randn(1,50,3).astype(np.float32) ini3=np.array([[15]]) end3=np.array([[40]]) y3=ov_compiled_model(x3, ini3, end3) print(f"Openvino-2: {y3}
")    Relevant log output RuntimeError                              Traceback (most recent call last) Cell In[3], line 12       9 del ov_model      11 config = {"INFERENCE_PRECISION_HINT": 'f32'} ---> 12 ov_compiled_model = ov.compile_model('model_simple.xml', "CPU", config=config)      14 x2=np.random.randn(1,10,3).astype(np.float32)      15 ini2=np.array([[2]])   File ~/miniconda3/envs/my_env/lib/python3.8/site-packages/openvino/runtime/ie_api.py:609, in compile_model(model, device_name, config)     593 """Compact method to compile model with AUTO plugin.     594      595 :param model: Model acquired from read_model function or a path to a model in IR / ONNX / PDPD /    (...)     606      607 """     608 core = Core() --> 609 return core.compile_model(model, device_name, {} if config is None else config)      File ~/miniconda3/envs/my_env/lib/python3.8/site-packages/openvino/runtime/ie_api.py:521, in Core.compile_model(self, model, device_name, config, weights)     516     if device_name is None:     517         return CompiledModel(     518             super().compile_model(model, {} if config is None else config),     519         )     520     return CompiledModel( ... Exception from src/plugins/intel_cpu/src/node.cpp:87: Unexpected: CPU plug-in doesn't support If operation with dynamic rank. Operation name: /If Issue submission checklist   I'm reporting an issue. It's not a question.  I checked the problem with the documentation, FAQ, open issues, Stack Overflow, etc., and have not found a solution.  There is reproducer code and related data files such as images, videos, models, etc.
